WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.543
Hi, friends. This is Brave Enough to Ask.

00:00:12.543 --> 00:00:17.087
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:17.087 --> 00:00:19.813
Hands flat on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:19.813 --> 00:00:22.539
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:22.539 --> 00:00:27.991
Everybody gets stuck sometimes — even teachers, even grown-ups.

00:00:27.991 --> 00:00:35.260
Being stuck is nothing to hide. It is a signal: time to ask for help.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:40.712
And asking for help is not weak. Asking is brave.

00:00:40.712 --> 00:00:51.616
Here is the way: notice you're stuck, choose who to ask, say it simply, and thank your helper.

00:00:51.616 --> 00:00:58.885
Let's practice with a pretend moment: you're reading, and one word just will not make sense.

00:00:58.885 --> 00:01:07.063
First — notice you're stuck. You read it again… and again. Shoulders tight. That tight feeling is the signal.

00:01:07.063 --> 00:01:12.515
Next — choose who to ask. Your teacher is right there, ready to help.

00:01:12.515 --> 00:01:18.876
Now say it in simple words: "I need help with this word, please."

00:01:18.876 --> 00:01:29.780
Your teacher shows you. You read the word, and the story makes sense again. Thank your helper: "Thank you for helping me."

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:37.049
One more. Pretend the lid of your water bottle is stuck tight — too tight to turn.

00:01:37.049 --> 00:01:43.409
Notice you're stuck. Choose who to ask — a classmate beside you has strong hands.

00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:49.770
Say it simply: "I need help opening this, please." They hold; you turn together. It opens.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:55.222
Thank them: "Thanks for helping me." It worked — because you were brave enough to ask.

00:01:55.222 --> 00:02:01.583
Notice. Choose. Say it simply. Thank your helper. That is Brave Enough to Ask.

00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:07.035
When you ask, you give someone a gift too: the chance to be kind.

00:02:07.035 --> 00:02:11.578
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:11.578 --> 00:02:15.213
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:15.213 --> 00:02:18.847
You're ready for what's next.
